## Traffic Flow

| Direction | Protocol | Purpose |
|-----------|----------|---------|
| Attacker-Box → Linux-Endpoint | SSH | Brute-force simulation |
| Attacker-Box → Windows-Endpoint | RDP | Brute-force simulation |
| Attacker-Box → Either endpoint | TCP various | Port scanning |
| Linux-Endpoint → SOC-SIEM | Wazuh agent (1514) | Log collection |
| Windows-Endpoint → SOC-SIEM | Wazuh agent (1514) | Log collection |
| macOS → SOC-SIEM | HTTPS 443 | Dashboard access |

## Data Collection Points

| VM | Data Source | Collected By |
|---|---|---|
| Linux-Endpoint | /var/log/auth.log | Wazuh agent |
| Linux-Endpoint | /var/log/ufw.log | Wazuh agent |
| Linux-Endpoint | /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow | Wazuh FIM |
| Linux-Endpoint | /opt/important/* | Wazuh FIM |
| Windows-Endpoint | Security Event ID 4625, 4624 | Wazuh agent (eventchannel) |
| Windows-Endpoint | PowerShell Event ID 4104 | Wazuh agent |
| Windows-Endpoint | Sysmon Event ID 1, 3 | Wazuh agent |
| Windows-Endpoint | Defender Operational log | Wazuh agent |
| SOC-SIEM | All agent events | Wazuh indexer |
| SOC-SIEM | Alert rules | Wazuh manager |

## Resource Allocation (8 GB RAM Mac)

| Running Scenario | VMs Active | Total RAM | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Wazuh setup | SOC-SIEM only | 4 GB | Comfortable |
| Linux testing | SOC-SIEM + Linux-Endpoint | 5-5.5 GB | Comfortable |
| Linux attack simulation | SOC-SIEM + Linux + Attacker | 6-7 GB | Near limit |
| Windows testing | SOC-SIEM + Windows-Endpoint | 6-7 GB | Close other apps |
| Windows attack simulation | SOC-SIEM + Windows + Attacker | 7-8 GB | Tight; close everything else |
| Cross-platform | SOC-SIEM + Linux + Windows | 7-8 GB | Very tight; avoid |

**Rule:** Never run Linux-Endpoint and Windows-Endpoint at the same time as the Attacker-Box. Pick one platform per session.

