## Security Boundaries

| Boundary | Control |
|----------|---------|
| Lab ↔ Internet | UTM Shared NAT; limited outbound |
| Attacker ↔ Targets | Allowed; this is the test traffic |
| SIEM ↔ Endpoints | Agent authentication; encrypted agent communication |
| Host ↔ VMs | Browser HTTPS only; no VM file sharing |
| Windows RDP | Disabled externally in production; RDP exposed only inside lab |

## Scaling Considerations

| If you add... | Impact | Mitigation |
|---------------|--------|------------|
| Second Linux endpoint | +1 GB RAM | Only for specific multi-target scenarios |
| pfSense later | Requires emulation; very slow | Not recommended on this hardware |
| Additional SIEM | Wazuh is already heavy | Do not run Splunk or Elastic alongside |
| More Windows endpoints | +2-3 GB each | Test one at a time; shut down others |
